#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/mt.rc -- Maltese (Malti), the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "mt"`.
//
// Stage E109, group B. Adapted, not translated word for word (decision 198.14): the source of the
// sense is en.rc and ru.rc, the place and the room of every string is res/lang/context.tsv, the
// words of the program are in l10n/glossary/mt.tsv of the control contour. The site side is
// English (GitHub Issues, as en.rc). The reader is addressed in the singular imperative (it has
// no gender in Maltese); the author speaks in the masculine ("kuntent"). The article il- becomes
// like the next sound before the sun letters (ċ d n r s t x ż z): ix-, it-, is-, iċ-...
//
// In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Maltese — `[general] language = "mt"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
